                       We Have The Firstname , Lastname & We Can Notice Its Present In "Person" Table And
                       City , State Which Is In "Address" Table . 
                       
                       Now The Question Is Telling Us That If There Is Person Id In Person Table Whose Address Is Not Mentioned
                       In The Address Table Then We Have To Report This As "Null" In Output .
                       

                       So As We Can See In The Person Table That We Have Two Person Id Which Are 
                       1 --- Alice & 2 --- Bob And As We Go & Check In The Address Table For Both Of Them It Is Noticed That 
                      The Address Mentioned As New York City Is For Person Id 2 Which Is Bob But There Is No Record Of The 
                      Address For Person Id 1 Which Is Alice So Now We Know That We Have To Report This Part As Null In Our 
                      Output . So We Have Our Final Answer Where We Have The Firstname , Lastname , City & State Which Is 
                      This Is What Our Final Output Will Atleast Look Like . 
                      
                      
                       Firstname | Lastname | City          | State
                       Alice     | Wang     | Null          | Null 
                       Bob       | Alice    | New York City | New York 
                      
                      
                      

                     Now Let's Talk About Our Query -----
                     [ select person.firstname , person.lastname , address.city , address.state ] Is In Order To Select The Respective
                     Data From Their Respective Tables As Firstanme , Lastname Are Mentioned In Person Table But City & State Are 
                     Mentioned In Address Table . [ From Person ] Means That We Are Starting With Person Table . [ Left Join Address ]
                     Means That We Are Using Left Join Function Here . Why ? Because The Question clearly Asks Us To Report 
                     firstname , Lastname , City & State Of "" Each Person In The Person Table "" Which Means We Need All Of 
                     The Data Of Person Table Along With That Only The Matching Rows From Another Table Which Is The Address Table Here . 
                     This Is The Main Reason Why We Use The Left Join Function Here In This Question . [ on person.personid = address.personid ] 
                     Means That We Are Joining Two Tables Person Table & Address Table On The Basis Of Person Id Which Is Common In
                     Both These Tables & Starting With [ person.person id ] Beacuse We Used Left Join Function So We Start With The Left Table . 
                      
